{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on e148a96e for NF-2 (9a321a0a).\n\nSize. Keep the schema inline, and do not try `$defs`. A `$defs`\nblock lives inside one tool's schema, so it cannot share\nACT_OUTPUT between the 59 act tools. Put your figures in the note:\n170,890 bytes at main 33836693, the bytes at the review head, and\nACT_OUTPUT at 1,854 bytes in 59 tools. NF-2 does no more work on\nsize.\n\nOne limit to state in the note: each new act tool adds its input\nschema and 1,854 bytes of output schema, and the whole list is 6\npercent under one page. The live window on the test Worker\nmeasures what a host puts in the model's context from this list.\nI own that measurement. A reduction waits for it.\n\nFaults. Fix both in NF-2, as you propose.\n1. `scopeRefArg` takes the parser's alphabet for the last\n   character. This is the case that scope item 3 names.\n2. The `settle` schema gains `membership`. Item 3 told you to list\n   this kind of difference and not to fix it. I rule that you fix\n   it, because a strict host refuses a settle call for a creation\n   today. Add one test that a settle call for a creation passes\n   the schema and the parser.\n\nList every other difference of the audit in the note, with no\nchange.\n\nThe first sandbox receipt: I take it at the next deployment, which\nnames all five Workers. I open no window for the sandbox alone.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}